                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mRemote Sens. 2022, 14, 2301\u001b[0m                                                                                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m2 of 25\u001b[0m                                                                                                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m1. Introduction\u001b[0m                                                                                                \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mThe frequency and intensity of severe precipitation events are expected to continue\u001b[0m                            \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mincreasing as a result of climate change [1,2]. In turn, precipitation-triggered disasters,\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mincluding landslides and ﬂoods, are also becoming more frequent [3]. Landslide early\u001b[0m                           \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mwarning systems (LEWSs) aim to reduce loss of life and damage, by giving people advanced\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mwarning so that emergency responders may prepare resources and warn the public to\u001b[0m                              \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mavoid high-risk areas [4]. Existing LEWSs rely on knowledge of past events in order to\u001b[0m                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mimprove the understanding of landslide triggering processes, develop warning thresholds\u001b[0m                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mand prediction models, and ﬁnally verify warnings issued and evaluate performance [5].\u001b[0m                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mLandslide inventory data are also needed to produce landslide susceptibility and hazard\u001b[0m                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mmaps used for spatial planning, and emergency responders need detailed information to\u001b[0m                          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32massess damages and save lives [6].\u001b[0m                                                                             \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mHowever, for operators of LEWSs, collecting landslide data and verifying warnings\u001b[0m                              \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mis a difﬁcult and tedious task [7]. Generally, the registration of events and preparation\u001b[0m                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mof landslide inventories are not performed systematically [8]. Presently, single-landslide\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mevent data are collected mainly from ground observations, including reports from road\u001b[0m                          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mand rail authorities, and to a lesser degree from the public, or mined from social media\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mand rail authorities, and to a lesser degree from the public, or mined from social media\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mand news reports [9,10]. For triggering events (e.g., extreme precipitation or earthquake)\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mwith multiple resulting landslides, mapping using aerial or satellite optical images may be\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mundertaken on a case-by-case basis, depending on motivation and resources [11–13]. Such\u001b[0m                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mmapping is most commonly limited to areas that are already known to have been affected\u001b[0m                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mby landslides (e.g., [14–16]), or to verify the exact location of landslides that may have\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mbeen reported without precise coordinates, for example, in media reports [17]. Systematic\u001b[0m                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mmapping is generally not yet carried out over large areas or to identify previously unknown\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mlandslides in remote areas.\u001b[0m                                                                                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mThe resulting landslide databases, however, tend to show clusters of observations\u001b[0m                              \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32maround linear infrastructure and populated areas, thus not giving a realistic representation\u001b[0m                   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mof the true spatial distribution of landslides, as can be seen in Figure 1. Additionally,\u001b[0m                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mlandslide inventories tend to be rather incomplete. For example, in Europe, a comparison\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mbetween landslide density based on landslide records from the Geological Surveys of\u001b[0m                            \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mEurope and the European landslide susceptibility map (ELSUS 1000 v1) reveals that only\u001b[0m                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mthree countries (Poland, Italy, and Slovakia) have inventories considered to be over 50%\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mcomplete [18]. These issues with spatial bias and missing data limit how the landslide data\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mPage 8:\u001b[0m                                                                                                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mRemote Sens. 2022, 14, 2301\u001b[0m                                                                                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m8 of 25\u001b[0m                                                                                                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mFigure 5. Study area showing landslides mapped with Sentinel-2 dNDVI images (orange polygons),\u001b[0m                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mregistered landslides (triangles; source: NLDB, 18 December 2019), and ground-truth locations,\u001b[0m                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mincluding drone survey areas (shaded light blue) and helicopter and ﬁeld visit GPS tracks (green and\u001b[0m           \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mblack dashed lines, respectively). Background: Sentinel-2 image.\u001b[0m                                               \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mThe landscape consists of U-shaped valleys with ﬂat, angled, polished bedrock surfaces\u001b[0m                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mthat are favourable for the formation of sliding planes. Other signatures of the strong linear,\u001b[0m                \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mglacial erosion in competent rock are visible in the area, including roche moutonnée, crag,\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mand tail features. These types of bedrock features are exposed in the upper half of the Jølster\u001b[0m                \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mlandscape. A few remnant small-scale brittle faults are visible in the landscape [41]. Most of\u001b[0m                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mthe study area has a surface cover of glacial moraine sediments [42]. The moraine is often\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mhighly consolidated on slopes overlying the bedrock. At high altitudes in the mountains,\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32msmall pockets of moraine can be found within depressions in the exposed bare bedrock.\u001b[0m                          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mA loose veneer of colluvium extends downslope on the valley sides, increasing to several\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mmetres thick at the valley bottom.\u001b[0m                                                                             \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mBuried hummus layers show evidence of previous landslides, seen in the stratigraphy\u001b[0m                            \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mexposed by a debris ﬂow at Slåtten (Figure 3B). There are at least 40 historical landslide\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mexposed by a debris ﬂow at Slåtten (Figure 3B). There are at least 40 historical landslide\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mevents registered as points in the Norwegian national landslide database (NLDB, at www.\u001b[0m                        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mskredregistering.no, accessed on 18 January 2022, hence referred to as registered events) in the\u001b[0m               \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mstudy area, and several instances of rock falls. Registered events are dated from 1625 to 2019.\u001b[0m                \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mThe majority of the registered events in the NLDB are derived from observations along the\u001b[0m                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mroad network.\u001b[0m                                                                                                  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mThe modern climate of the study area is temperate, with relatively mild winters and\u001b[0m                            \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mwet summers due to the proximity to the coast. Glaciers are still active in the region, with\u001b[0m                   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mJostedalsbreen National Park, located 30 km east of the study area. Vegetation in the study\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32marea ranges from sparse moss and shrubs or light birch forest at high elevations, to spruce\u001b[0m                    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
