                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mthe study area has a surface cover of glacial moraine sediments [42]. The moraine is often\u001b[0m                     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32mhighly consolidated on slopes overlying the bedrock. At high altitudes in the mountains,\u001b[0m                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                 \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[32msmall pockets of moraine can be found within depressions in the exposed bare bedrock.\u001b[0m                          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
