                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">Google Earth Engine\", \"method_type\": \"CUSTOM_CODE\", \"summary\": \"In GEE, separate pre- and post-event </span>          <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">Sentinel-2 level 2A image collections were produced by filtering the entire collection by location and date. </span>  <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">NDVI bands were added to all images, then 'greenest-pixel' pre- and post-event composite images were created </span>  <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">by taking the maximum NDVI value per pixel using the quality mosaic function. A difference image (dNDVI) was </span>  <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">produced by subtracting the pre-event composite from the post-event composite. This composite was then used </span>   <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">for visual/manual landslide detection and comparison against the S2-BT baseline inventory.\", \"code_status\": </span>   <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">\"FOUND\", \"code_link\": \"https://github.com/erin-ntnu/Change-detection-images-GEE\", \"reused_citation\": null}, </span>   <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">{\"name\": \"Sentinel-1 Bi-Temporal (S1-BT) enriched RGB backscatter change-detection composite\", \"method_type\":</span>  <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">\"REUSED\", \"summary\": \"Pre- and post-event Sentinel-1 SLC scenes (IW mode, VV/VH) were downloaded from COAH, </span>   <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">geocoded, orbit-corrected, noise-removed, multi-looked, and geocoded with a 10 m DTM to produce radar </span>         <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">backscatter images. To facilitate visual interpretation, multi-temporal change detection was applied using </span>    <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">enriched colour composites (R,G,B) = (pre, post, pre), stretched from [\\u221235,10] dB to [\\u221225,5] dB, </span>    <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">following an approach originally developed for snow-avalanche detection. The best of three composites (based </span>  <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">on different post-event dates) was manually selected for further (manual) landslide visibility analysis.\", </span>    <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">\"code_status\": \"N/A\", \"code_link\": null, \"reused_citation\": \"Approach for enriched RGB backscatter composites</span>  <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
                            "<span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>  <span style=\"color: #00ff00; text-decoration-color: #00ff00\">developed for snow-avalanche detection (references [43,44] in the paper)\"}, {\"name\": \"Sentinel-1 </span>              <span style=\"color: #008000; text-decoration-color: #008000\">│</span>\n",
