                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m{\"methods\": [{\"name\": \"Manual digitisation of landslides from Sentinel-2 Bi-Temporal (S2-BT) dNDVI composite \u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92min SNAP\", \"method_type\": \"MANUAL\", \"summary\": \"Preliminary landslide mapping was conducted using the \u001b[0m          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mconventional S2-BT approach. Pre- and post-event Level 2A Sentinel-2 tiles were processed in SNAP 7.0 \u001b[0m         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92msoftware (cropped, collocated, and band-math used to calculate dNDVI = (B8R\\u2212B4R)/(B8R+B4R) \\u2212 \u001b[0m        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m(B8S\\u2212B4S)/(B8S+B4S)). Polygons delimiting assumed landslides, typically represented by dark elongated \u001b[0m    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mclusters of pixels, were then drawn manually in SNAP. This preliminary mapping was completed within a week of\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mthe landslide occurrences and took approximately three hours; it was later verified and updated through field\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mvisits, a helicopter flight, and comparison with a detailed field map.\", \"code_status\": \"N/A\", \"code_link\": \u001b[0m   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mnull, \"reused_citation\": null}, {\"name\": \"Sentinel-2 Multi-Temporal (S2-MT) dNDVI composite generation in \u001b[0m     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mGoogle Earth Engine\", \"method_type\": \"CUSTOM_CODE\", \"summary\": \"In GEE, separate pre- and post-event \u001b[0m          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mSentinel-2 level 2A image collections were produced by filtering the entire collection by location and date. \u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mNDVI bands were added to all images, then 'greenest-pixel' pre- and post-event composite images were created \u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mby taking the maximum NDVI value per pixel using the quality mosaic function. A difference image (dNDVI) was \u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mproduced by subtracting the pre-event composite from the post-event composite. This composite was then used \u001b[0m   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mfor visual/manual landslide detection and comparison against the S2-BT baseline inventory.\", \"code_status\": \u001b[0m   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m\"FOUND\", \"code_link\": \"https://github.com/erin-ntnu/Change-detection-images-GEE\", \"reused_citation\": null}, \u001b[0m   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m{\"name\": \"Sentinel-1 Bi-Temporal (S1-BT) enriched RGB backscatter change-detection composite\", \"method_type\":\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m\"REUSED\", \"summary\": \"Pre- and post-event Sentinel-1 SLC scenes (IW mode, VV/VH) were downloaded from COAH, \u001b[0m   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mgeocoded, orbit-corrected, noise-removed, multi-looked, and geocoded with a 10 m DTM to produce radar \u001b[0m         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mbackscatter images. To facilitate visual interpretation, multi-temporal change detection was applied using \u001b[0m    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92menriched colour composites (R,G,B) = (pre, post, pre), stretched from [\\u221235,10] dB to [\\u221225,5] dB, \u001b[0m    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mfollowing an approach originally developed for snow-avalanche detection. The best of three composites (based \u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mon different post-event dates) was manually selected for further (manual) landslide visibility analysis.\", \u001b[0m    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m\"code_status\": \"N/A\", \"code_link\": null, \"reused_citation\": \"Approach for enriched RGB backscatter composites\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mdeveloped for snow-avalanche detection (references [43,44] in the paper)\"}, {\"name\": \"Sentinel-1 \u001b[0m              \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mMulti-Temporal (S1-MT) RGB backscatter composite generation in Google Earth Engine\", \"method_type\": \u001b[0m           \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92m\"CUSTOM_CODE\", \"summary\": \"Using GEE, pre-processed Sentinel-1 GRD scenes (calibrated and ortho-corrected via\u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mthe Sentinel-1 Toolbox) were filtered into separate pre- and post-event collections by location, date, \u001b[0m        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mpolarisation (VV, VH), acquisition geometry (ascending/descending mean combined via median), and acquisition \u001b[0m  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
                            "\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m  \u001b[92mmode (IW). A topographic correction function was applied using a 10 m DTM uploaded as a GEE asset. The two \u001b[0m    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\n",
