                        "text/plain": [
                            "'{\"datasets\":[{\"name\":\"Sentinel-1 SAR satellite imagery (C-band, VV/VH polarizations, GRD/SLC scenes)\",\"source\":\"European Space Agency (ESA) Copernicus programme\",\"link\":\"https://scihub.copernicus.eu/dhus/#/home\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Sentinel-2 multispectral optical satellite imagery (Level 2A, BOA reflectance)\",\"source\":\"European Space Agency (ESA) Copernicus programme\",\"link\":\"https://scihub.copernicus.eu/dhus/#/home\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Digital Terrain Model (DTM), 10 m resolution, used for terrain correction of SAR data\",\"source\":\"Høydedata (Norwegian national elevation data service)\",\"link\":\"https://hoydedata.no/LaserInnsyn/\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Registered/historic landslide inventory data (\\'Skredhendelser\\' point data with attributes) - Norwegian National Landslide Database (NLDB)\",\"source\":\"NVE (Norwegian Directorate of Water and Energy) and RegObs\",\"link\":\"https://nedlasting.nve.no/gis/\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Road network dataset (\\'Vbase\\' polyline data) used for spatial bias analysis\",\"source\":\"NMA (Norwegian Mapping Authority)\",\"link\":\"https://kartkatalog.geonorge.no/\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Detailed field-verified landslide inventory map (release, transport, deposition zones) produced via field investigations and drone orthophotos\",\"source\":\"Co-author D. Rüther, field surveys and drone photography (also referenced in a separate report/manuscript, ref. [36])\",\"link\":null,\"status\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Field survey photographs and helicopter/GPS verification data from Jølster landslide site visits (Aug/Oct 2019, and 2020 field seasons)\",\"source\":\"Authors\\' own fieldwork (NGI, NGU, HVL co-authors)\",\"link\":null,\"status\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Bedrock geology reference map used for geomorphological description of study area\",\"source\":\"Norges Geologiske Undersøkelse (NGU) - Norwegian Geological Survey\",\"link\":\"https://geo.ngu.no/kart/berggrunn_mobil/\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"},{\"name\":\"Google Earth Engine (GEE) processing scripts for generating Sentinel-1/2 change detection composites (code/methodology, not raw data)\",\"source\":\"Authors (Erin Lindsay et al.), hosted on GitHub\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/erin-ntnu/Change-detection-images-GEE\",\"status\":\"AVAILABLE\"}],\"methods\":[{\"name\":\"Manual visual interpretation and digitisation of landslide polygons from change-detection composites\",\"method_type\":\"MANUAL\",\"summary\":\"Landslide polygons were drawn manually (by expert interpreters) by visually inspecting the four different pre-/post-event change-detection image composites (S2-BT, S2-MT, S1-BT, S1-MT). Polygons delimiting assumed landslides, typically dark elongated clusters of pixels, were digitised in SNAP; the initial S2-BT inventory was subsequently verified and refined through field visits, a helicopter flight, and comparison with a detailed field map produced by a co-author, then used as the baseline for systematically searching for the same landslides in the other three composite images.\",\"code_status\":\"N/A\",\"code_link\":null,\"reused_citation\":null},{\"name\":\"Sentinel-2 Bi-Temporal (S2-BT) dNDVI change-detection image production using SNAP software\",\"method_type\":\"SOFTWARE\",\"summary\":\"Level 2A Sentinel-2 tiles from before/after the event were downloaded from COAH, cropped, co-registered, and processed in SNAP 7.0 using the band-math tool to compute a bi-temporal difference NDVI (dNDVI) image (dNDVI = NDVI_post − NDVI_pre) using bands B8 (NIR) and B4 (red). This produced the conventional bi-temporal image used for the preliminary manual mapping.\",\"code_status\":\"N/A\",\"code_link\":null,\"reused_citation\":null},{\"name\":\"Sentinel-2 Multi-Temporal (S2-MT) NDVI composite generation using Google Earth Engine script\",\"method_type\":\"CUSTOM_CODE\",\"summary\":\"In Google Earth Engine (GEE), separate pre- and post-event Sentinel-2 Level 2A image collections were filtered by location/date, NDVI bands were added, and \\'greenest-pixel\\' composites were created using the quality-mosaic function (taking the maximum NDVI per pixel across one month of images). A difference image (dNDVI) was then produced by subtracting the pre-event composite from the post-event composite. This custom multi-temporal compositing procedure was implemented as a GEE script.\",\"code_status\":\"FOUND\",\"code_link\":\"https://github.com/erin-ntnu/Change-detection-images-GEE\",\"reused_citation\":null},{\"name\":\"Sentinel-1 Bi-Temporal (S1-BT) SAR backscatter/RGB composite production using SNAP/Sentinel-1 Toolbox\",\"method_type\":\"SOFTWARE\",\"summary\":\"Pre- and post-event Sentinel-1 SLC scenes (VV, VH, IW mode) were downloaded from COAH and processed with standard SAR pre-processing steps (orbit-state vector refinement, atmospheric noise removal, multi-looking, geocoding with a 10 m DTM) to produce backscatter GeoTIFF images. Enriched RGB colour composites (R,G,B = pre, post, pre) were then created following an approach originally developed for snow-avalanche detection, using existing SAR processing software/toolboxes (e.g., Sentinel-1 Toolbox) rather than custom analysis code.\",\"code_status\":\"N/A\",\"code_link\":null,\"reused_citation\":\"RGB enrichment approach adapted from prior snow-avalanche detection studies (references [43,44] in the paper)\"},{\"name\":\"Sentinel-1 Multi-Temporal (S1-MT) mean VV/VH composite generation using Google Earth Engine script\",\"method_type\":\"CUSTOM_CODE\",\"summary\":\"Using GEE, pre-processed Sentinel-1 GRD scenes (calibrated/ortho-corrected via the Sentinel-1 Toolbox) were filtered into separate pre- and post-event collections by location, date, polarisation (VV, VH), acquisition geometry, and mode (IW). A topographic correction function was applied using a 10 m DTM GEE asset, the collections were reduced to mean images, and RGB composites were built (pre-event in red/green channels, post-event in blue) for each polarisation. This multi-temporal compositing and correction pipeline was implemented as a custom GEE script.\",\"code_status\":\"FOUND\",\"code_link\":\"https://github.com/erin-ntnu/Change-detection-images-GEE\",\"reused_citation\":null}],\"availability\":{\"access_status\":\"NOT_ACCESSIBLE\",\"data_status\":\"NOT_STATED\",\"data_links\":[],\"code_status\":\"NOT_STATED\",\"code_links\":[],\"author_statement\":\"The publication page could not be accessed (HTTP 403 error when attempting to reach https://doi.org/10.3390/rs14102301, which redirects to https://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/14/10/2301). No content, including any Data Availability Statement or Code Availability Statement, could be retrieved or verified from this attempt.\"},\"reproducibility_assessment\":\"Partially reproducible: most satellite and ancillary datasets (Sentinel-1/2, DTM, landslide inventory, road network, bedrock geology) are named with public retrieval links and are available, and GEE scripts for the custom multi-temporal composite generation (S2-MT, S1-MT) are found on GitHub. However, key elements are missing or unverifiable — the detailed field-verified landslide inventory map and field survey/photographic data are not available, the manual interpretation/digitisation method and SNAP-based bi-temporal processing (S2-BT, S1-BT) have no associated code, and the publisher\\'s page could not be accessed to confirm any formal data/code availability statement. Overall, reproducibility is limited: core input data are largely accessible, some custom code is available, but manual/expert-driven steps and certain reference datasets lack accessible artifacts, and no verifiable author statement on availability exists.\"}'"
